Subject: [PATCH] d3d10umd: keep the offset in dynamically indexed immediate constant buffer reads

An operand icb[r + n] (D3D10_SB_OPERAND_INDEX_IMMEDIATE32_PLUS_RELATIVE on
D3D10_SB_OPERAND_TYPE_IMMEDIATE_CONSTANT_BUFFER) added n to a copy of the
immediate block register and then built the indirect source from the
unmodified sx->imms, so the read returned icb[r] instead of icb[r + n].
fxc packs several static const arrays into one immediate constant buffer
and addresses the later ones with an offset: SubD11's SmoothPS keeps four
light directions at icb[0..3] and four light colours at icb[4..7] and reads
icb[r2.w + 4] in its light loop, so every light colour was a direction and
the model rendered purple and speckled. Build the indirect source from the
offset register.

probes/d3d11-tess/tess_probe.exe (value 17) runs the same loop and compares
it with the CPU result.

Evidence: docs/d3d11-apps.md, docs/evidence/d3d11-apps/.
Origin: vmlab-win3d fix-d3d11-apps worker.
---
diff --git a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/ShaderTGSI.c b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/ShaderTGSI.c
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/ShaderTGSI.c
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/ShaderTGSI.c
@@ -2774,10 +2774,11 @@
          break;
       case D3D10_SB_OPERAND_INDEX_RELATIVE:
       case D3D10_SB_OPERAND_INDEX_IMMEDIATE32_PLUS_RELATIVE:
+         /* icb[r + n]: keep the immediate offset n. */
          reg = sx->imms;
          reg.Index += operand->base.index[0].imm;
          reg = ureg_src_indirect(
-            sx->imms,
+            reg,
             translate_relative_operand(sx, &operand->base.index[0].rel));
          break;
       default:
